**Inline callbacks in `components/app/ChatInterface.js` (lines 371–382, 414)**

Every render creates new function references, causing child re-renders.

```jsx
// Problem — new function on every render
<button onClick={() => {
  updateDocumentData({ state: state.code });
  setMessages(prev => [...prev, ...]);
}}>

// Fix — memoize with useCallback
const handleStateSelect = useCallback((stateCode) => {
  updateDocumentData({ state: stateCode });
  setMessages(prev => [...prev, { type: 'bot', content: ... }]);
}, [updateDocumentData]);

<button onClick={() => handleStateSelect(state.code)}>
```

**Inline style objects in `components/app/EditorView.js` (lines 56, 435, 451, 467)**

```jsx
// Problem — new object every render
<div style={{ width: `${chatWidth}%` }}>

// Fix — memoize
const layoutStyles = useMemo(() => ({
  chat: { width: `${chatWidth}%` },
  preview: { width: `${previewWidth}%` },
}), [chatWidth, previewWidth]);
<div style={layoutStyles.chat}>
```

---

**`app/api/catalog/matters/route.ts` — static data served without caching**

```typescript
// Problem
export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic'; // cache miss every request

// Fix — ISR with stale-while-revalidate
export const revalidate = 3600;

return NextResponse.json(
  { success: true, data: { matters } },
  { headers: { 'Cache-Control': 'public, s-maxage=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400' } }
);
```

**`app/api/templates/states/route.ts` — same pattern, same fix.** `getSupportedStates()` returns static data. Add `export const revalidate = 3600` and matching `Cache-Control` header.

Both routes serve read-only data that never changes between deploys. These are the highest-impact fixes — zero code complexity, big latency reduction for repeat visitors.

---

**`components/app/CountyValidationInput.js` line 202** — `setTimeout` in an event handler with no cleanup:

```jsx
// Problem
onBlur={() => { setTimeout(() => setShowSuggestions(false), 200); }}

// Fix — track and cancel
const blurTimeoutRef = useRef(null);
onBlur={() => {
  blurTimeoutRef.current = setTimeout(() => setShowSuggestions(false), 200);
}}
useEffect(() => () => clearTimeout(blurTimeoutRef.current), []);
```

**`components/app/AffidavitForm.js` lines 295–300** — same pattern for the save-status clear timeout. Same fix: store in a ref and clear on unmount.

---

**`components/app/ChatInterface.js` lines 75–83** — `generateFactSignature` runs `JSON.stringify` on the full facts array on every summary check:

```jsx
// Problem — called repeatedly, O(n) on every render
const generateFactSignature = (facts) => JSON.stringify(
  facts.map(f => typeof f === 'string' ? f : f.content)
);

// Fix — memoize with useMemo so it only recomputes when facts change
const factSignature = useMemo(
  () => JSON.stringify(facts.map(f => typeof f === 'string' ? f : f.content)),
  [facts]
);
```

